@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title claudecode paradigm — ML blackbox algorithm (spec → plan → implement → verify → loop)

actor "Developer\ngoal + stopping condition" as DEV

node "claudecode container" as CTR <<host>> {
  component "defs/claudecode/mcp/entrypoint.sh" as EP <<app>>
  component "claude --dangerously-skip-permissions" as CLI <<error>>
  artifact "CLAUDE.md\nloop pattern + acceptance criteria" as MD <<db>>
  component "verification commands\n(internal/verify preamble)" as VER <<app>>
  database "/workspace/input (repo)\n/workspace/output (artifacts)" as WS <<db>>
}

DEV ARROW_MAIN CLI : goal
EP ARROW_MAIN MD : seed when absent
EP ARROW_MAIN VER
EP ARROW_MAIN CLI : " ""ANTHROPIC_MODEL"" \n""ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL"" (bare ids) "
CLI ARROW_MAIN WS : implement
CLI ARROW_MAIN VER : verify
VER ARROW_MAIN CLI : loop until acceptance criteria met
CLI ARROW_MAIN DEV : stops on the stated condition

note right of CLI
  **The dangerous flag is deliberate** — and is only
  acceptable because containment is external: hardened
  container + enforced egress + credential broker
  (_spec/_paradigms/egress-boundary.puml,
   _spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary.puml).
  Nothing here relies on the model's restraint.

  Small verifiable loops beat large open-ended tasks;
  errors are expected — the value is fast iteration
  inside the loop.
end note

note bottom of WS
  ""layout: input-output"" — the only harness that does not
  use ""/app"". ""/workspace"" itself is **not** a mount, so a
  path outside ""input""/""output"" is written into the
  container's ephemeral layer and lost on exit.
end note

note bottom of EP
  Variants share this paradigm: ""mcp"" is the **default**
  image (""proveo/claudecode""); ""solidity"" layers the EVM
  contract toolchain (Foundry · solc · solhint · semgrep)
  **on top of mcp** — the heaviest variant; ""-browser"" is
  mcp FROM base-node-browser (Playwright + Chromium).

  Subscription harness: proveo warns rather than prompts
  when ""CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN"" is absent and lets the
  agent handle login.
end note

note right of CLI
  **No DinD.** Alone in the fleet, claudecode ships no
  docker client and stays ""dind: false"": the privileged
  sibling is ""broker""-mode only, and this is the harness
  whose permission posture depends on the boundary that
  mode removes. Container work stays deferred to the
  per-sandbox engine in
  _spec/_experiments/docker-sandbox.puml
  (Cursor-led experiment; claudecode is secondary).
end note
@enduml
